speechtext:
I find it most difficult to know how to deal with it because it seems to me it can only be based on a deliberate refusal to appreciate the meaning of words. Let us go through the section clause by clause. Section 33(1) says;
In any prosecution for a violation of subsection 2 of section 32, if the accused does not plead guilty, the trial shall proceed as if the issue to be tried is whether the accused was in possession of a controlled drug.
Very well. The issue to be tried is the issue of possession. The section does nothing to remove from the crown the onus of proof that is on the crown in every criminal case to prove the facts which it alleges or which are in issue as establishing the guilt of the accused.
